course: dictionary
lesson: 7484
title: Possess and its many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: «Possess» is a formal word for «have» or «own». When you read it, ask: is someone owning a thing, having a skill, or being taken over by a feeling or spirit? The words around it give the clue.
explain: The Emperor said China possessed «all things», so possess means had or owned. In another story, a character is «possessed», which means taken over, as if a spirit controls the mind. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: The question «What possessed you?» is informal. It does not ask who owns something. It means «Why on earth did you do that?» Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Possess is a verb, so its forms are possess, possesses, possessed and possessing.
fact: «Possess» means to own or have something, or to have a quality or skill.
fact: «Possessed» can mean taken over by a spirit or feeling, as in ghost stories.
fact: «What possessed you?» means «Why on earth did you do that?»
fact: The phrase «in possession of» means having or owning something, as in «in possession of the keys».
exercise: The Emperor said China possessed «all things» and needed no British goods. What does possessed mean here? | Broke into pieces | Wanted to buy | *Had or owned | Lost on a long journey
exercise: The story says, «He is now possessed.» What does possessed mean here? | Very pleased with a new toy | Fast asleep in bed | *Taken over, as if by a spirit | Lost in thought
exercise: Your friend jumps into the cold lake in January. You ask, «What possessed you?» What do you mean? | Where did you buy your swimsuit? | *Why on earth did you do that? | Who owns this lake? | Can I have a turn too?
test: Lily possesses a rare skill for drawing. What does possesses mean here? | *Has | Sells | Loses | Forgets
test: Which phrase means having or owning something? | Stay quiet | Out of breath | *In possession of | Under the weather
exam: Choose the best word: The old house seemed to ___ the boy's mind, and he could not stop thinking about the ghost. | Visit | Paint | Forget | *Possess
